{
  "schema": "k01.requirement_allocation_registry.v1",
  "project": "K01",
  "purpose": "Make allocation from system/interface requirements to assemblies, interfaces, parts and product characteristics explicit. Allocation never changes the upstream requirement text and never merges different physical quantities because their numeric values happen to match.",
  "rules": [
    "Every requirement that drives a part characteristic, derived engineering input or release test must have at least one allocation record before release.",
    "Allocation may be FULL, SHARED_COMPLEMENTARY, BUDGETED or FUNCTIONAL. Percentage shares are used only when physically meaningful; otherwise responsibility is stated qualitatively.",
    "Shared interface requirements allocate complementary responsibilities to each participant; they are not copied into one part as if that part alone owned the requirement.",
    "A requirement allocation is not a derived load and not a product characteristic. These are separate object classes with separate IDs and revisions.",
    "Changing an allocation invalidates downstream decisions/characteristics for every affected target and triggers counterpart review for shared interfaces."
  ],
